da319dfd-4982-4133-aab5-c833652a8ef1	96852b92-5684-4152-90b3-b07c249cb9ca	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	OpenAI has launched an enhanced ChatGPT Images experience along with the GPT-Image-1.5 model available via API. The update introduces ChatGPT Images 2.5, offering faster and improved image generation capabilities.	- Introduction of a faster ChatGPT Images experience.\n- Release of GPT-Image-1.5 model accessible through API.\n- Launch of ChatGPT Images 2.5 with improved features.	This update significantly enhances image generation capabilities within ChatGPT, improving speed and accessibility via API, which impacts developers and users leveraging AI-generated images.	\N	2026-11-10 14:11:42.425048+00	2026-11-10 14:11:42.425051+00
86ff145e-b79a-4f50-8a0a-6ed449fc676f	6ec7e352-5f09-4a4e-94ad-bac2397649d1	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	This research validates the hypothesis that language models internally represent archetypal relational patterns separately from subject domains and languages. Using the Qwen3.8-27B model, the study identifies distinct neuron groups encoding archetypes, topics, and languages, revealing a layered 'sandwich' structure that emerges spontaneously during training and underpins the model's intelligence and analogy capabilities.	- Language models hold archetypal relational patterns distinct from subject domains and languages.\n- Neurons are organized in layers: outer layers encode languages, inner layers encode topics, and core layers encode archetypes.\n- Silencing neurons related to archetypes or topics selectively removes pattern recognition or topic identification without affecting the other.\n- This layered 'sandwich' structure emerges spontaneously during pretraining and is consistent across models.\n- Archetypes serve as the architecture for analogy and are proposed as the mechanism behind language model intelligence.\n- The neurons, texts, and code used in the study are publicly released for reproducibility.	The study reveals a fundamental and interpretable internal structure in language models that explains how they represent knowledge and perform analogy, advancing understanding of AI intelligence mechanisms.	\N	2026-11-10 12:58:03.39812+00	2026-11-10 12:58:03.398123+00
