5c71f292-470c-48bf-a084-211075174abd	dfb70126-bc5e-464c-a01e-a9d902ef3137	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	The paper introduces Duet, a training-free dual-sparse inference framework for diffusion language models that reduces inference costs by leveraging prefix key-value sparsity and early query sparsity. Duet achieves significant speedups in end-to-end and per-step inference while maintaining competitive accuracy on models like LLaDA2.1-mini and SDAR-8B-Chat-b32 with long context lengths.	- Duet addresses costly inference in diffusion language models caused by repeated attention over growing historical prefixes and full processing of current generation blocks.\n- It uses prefix key-value sparsity to reuse a compact historical KV subset across denoising steps.\n- Early query sparsity predicts update positions and propagates only necessary queries through suffix Transformer layers, reducing computation.\n- Experiments demonstrate 1.34x to 2.83x speedups on LLaDA2.1-mini and 2.41x to 4.72x on SDAR-8B-Chat-b32 at 32K context length with maintained accuracy.	Duet presents a significant advancement in improving inference efficiency for diffusion language models, enabling faster generation with long context lengths without sacrificing accuracy, which is critical for scaling and practical deployment.	\N	2026-11-10 15:37:23.198658+00	2026-11-10 15:37:23.198662+00
