e03af041-c679-48fe-abdd-346367a84772	7ddab2c1-1f6c-4467-bc70-7edaaa2f4f85	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	PhoPunct presents a large-scale benchmark for Vietnamese punctuation restoration using 17 Transformer-based architectures evaluated on a dataset of 22.1 million labeled tokens. The study finds that adding Bi-LSTM and CRF layers does not consistently improve performance under a fixed training budget, with plain Transformer classifiers often matching or outperforming more complex models.	- Introduced a large-scale Vietnamese punctuation restoration benchmark with 22.1 million labeled tokens from News and Novels corpora.\n- Evaluated 17 architectures combining four pretrained Transformer backbones with optional Bi-LSTM and CRF layers under uniform training conditions.\n- Found that adding Bi-LSTM and CRF layers rarely improves macro F1 scores compared to plain Transformer classifiers.\n- PhoPunct (PhoBERT-large-Bi-LSTM-CRF) achieved the best result on News data, while XLM-R with CRF performed best on Novels data.\n- Results highlight the importance of separating architectural improvements from architecture-specific tuning effects.	Provides a significant large-scale benchmark and insights into the effectiveness of architectural choices for Vietnamese punctuation restoration, relevant for NLP research and model development.	\N	2026-11-10 15:37:02.336416+00	2026-11-10 15:37:02.336419+00
