34df0b2f-e239-43f5-ab31-4a392bcc7998	3518e97e-f4fd-45fb-8ee2-5c2aac7affb1	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	The paper introduces APEX, a two-stage retrieval framework for spoken language understanding that improves intent detection by first selecting candidate intents via prototypes and then retrieving contextual exemplars. Experiments on the SLURP dataset show that APEX significantly improves Exact Match Accuracy compared to query-based retrieval, especially under challenging conditions such as high-perplexity inputs and ASR-generated transcripts.	- APEX uses intent-level prototypes for candidate intent selection followed by exemplar retrieval within the selected intent space.\n- APEX improves Exact Match Accuracy by over 4 percentage points on full transcripts compared to query-based retrieval using Qwen3 4B and Gemma-3-4B models.\n- Under high-perplexity inputs, APEX yields even larger gains in accuracy, demonstrating robustness.\n- Prototype-guided candidate selection achieves higher ground truth intent coverage across various input conditions.	This research presents a relevant improvement in spoken language understanding by enhancing intent detection accuracy through a novel retrieval framework, which can impact applications relying on robust SLU.	\N	2026-11-10 15:37:39.221985+00	2026-11-10 15:37:39.221987+00
