070ea17e-211f-4e22-be9d-79af452adca2	c4d67280-d517-4665-87ab-c5b597e5485a	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	RuACT is a novel approach in rubric-based reinforcement learning that addresses the issue of inactive rubrics, which provide no learning signal due to being either unreachable or saturated. By treating unreachable rubrics as teachers and decomposing saturated rubrics into child rubrics as critics, RuACT improves learning performance on medical and scientific benchmarks using Qwen3 models.	- Inactive rubrics (unreachable or saturated) cause lack of learning signals in rubric-based RL.\n- RuACT assigns unreachable rubrics as teachers for reward-gated self-distillation and saturated rubrics as critics by decomposing them into child rubrics.\n- RuACT outperforms existing methods like GRPO and rubric reweighting on multiple benchmarks with Qwen3-4B and Qwen3-1.7B models.\n- Recovery of initially unreachable rubrics improved from 35.02% to 42.86%, and reward-quality alignment improved from 57.74% to 60.77%.\n- Code for RuACT is publicly available.	RuACT presents a significant advancement in rubric-based reinforcement learning by effectively recovering inactive rubrics, which enhances learning signals and improves performance on challenging medical and scientific tasks.	\N	2026-11-10 15:37:53.719065+00	2026-11-10 15:37:53.719068+00
