afce2be1-6995-4c73-a0c7-9a05707a9d08	0f05324b-c178-49ee-9070-aa57e85faf7b	openai/gpt-4.1-mini	en	The paper proposes SteganoPrompt, an input-side watermarking technique embedding invisible instructions into assignment prompts to detect verbatim copy-paste responses from large language models (LLMs). This method aims to provide educators with a reliable, model-agnostic way to identify unengaged use of LLMs, overcoming limitations of existing AI-text detectors and output-side watermarks.	- SteganoPrompt embeds invisible instructions in assignment prompts using Unicode Tags to create a watermark in LLM outputs.\n- The watermark survives common copy-paste channels and is tokenized as normal text by most LLMs.\n- The tool is zero-dependency, transparent, includes an academic integrity reminder, and is ethically designed for classroom use.\n- Evaluations were conducted across eight LLM families and various educational content channels.\n- Released under MIT license and publicly available at the provided URL.	This research introduces a novel, practical approach to detect verbatim LLM-generated responses in educational settings, addressing a significant challenge in AI ethics and academic integrity.	\N	2026-11-10 15:38:26.2828+00	2026-11-10 15:38:26.282803+00
