2bb534fd-8258-458d-8652-61eddede30fc	c9402267-ab70-45fa-b843-f47b6189bd14	\N	https://research.google/blog/google-research-at-the-check-up-from-healthcare-innovation-to-real-world-care-settings/	Google Research at The Check Up: from healthcare innovation to real-world care settings	https://research.google/blog/google-research-at-the-check-up-from-healthcare-innovation-to-real-world-care-settings/	https://research.google/blog/google-research-at-the-check-up-from-healthcare-innovation-to-real-world-care-settings/	\N	Health & Bioscience	Health & Bioscience	news	en	2026-03-17 19:47:00+00	2026-11-09 17:12:41.150117+00	4	\N	52daea832d35d9b11150c5307dc074ffb76b723903933229a4703c1a077f9d04	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:41.15069+00	2026-11-10 14:18:25.465367+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
9356dad2-4556-4fbc-aa9e-9d65f8382cf7	928ad6da-fec1-474b-ae1a-3cf781cb4d3e	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2602.23903v2	SegMate: Asymmetric Attention-Based Lightweight Architecture for Efficient Multi-Organ Segmentation	https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23903	https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23903	Andrei-Alexandru Bunea, Dan-Matei Popovici, Radu Tudor Ionescu	arXiv:2602.23903v2 Announce Type: replace-cross \nAbstract: State-of-the-art models for medical image segmentation achieve excellent accuracy, but require substantial computational resources, limiting deployment in typical resource-constrained clinical settings. We present SegMate, an efficient 2.5D framework that achieves state-of-the-art accuracy, while considerably reducing computational requirements. Our efficient design is the result of meticulously integrating asymmetric architectures, attention mechanisms, multi-scale feature fusion, slice-based positional conditioning, and multi-task optimization. We demonstrate the efficiency-accuracy trade-off of our framework across three modern backbones (EfficientNetV2-M, MambaOut-Tiny, FastViT-T12). We perform experiments on three datasets: TotalSegmentator, SegTHOR and AMOS22. Compared with the vanilla models, SegMate reduces computation (GFLOPs) by up to 2.5x and memory footprint (VRAM) by up to 2.1x, while generally registering performance gains of around 1%. On TotalSegmentator, we achieve a Dice score of 93.51% with only 295 MB peak GPU memory. Zero-shot cross-dataset evaluations on SegTHOR and AMOS22 demonstrate strong generalization, with Dice scores of up to 86.85% and 89.35%, respectively. SegMate variants in this study empower single GPU setups to process up to 10,000 volumes per hour with just 74 J per volume using batch inference, enabling population-scale CT processing on commodity hardware. We release our open-source code at https://github.com/andreibunea99/SegMate.	arXiv:2602.23903v2 Announce Type: replace-cross \nAbstract: State-of-the-art models for medical image segmentation achieve excellent accuracy, but require substantial computational resources, limiting deployment in typical resource-constrained clinical settings. We present SegMate, an efficient 2.5D framework that achieves state-of-the-art accuracy, while considerably reducing computational requirements. Our efficient design is the result of meticulously integrating asymmetric architectures, attention mechanisms, multi-scale feature fusion, slice-based positional conditioning, and multi-task optimization. We demonstrate the efficiency-accuracy trade-off of our framework across three modern backbones (EfficientNetV2-M, MambaOut-Tiny, FastViT-T12). We perform experiments on three datasets: TotalSegmentator, SegTHOR and AMOS22. Compared with the vanilla models, SegMate reduces computation (GFLOPs) by up to 2.5x and memory footprint (VRAM) by up to 2.1x, while generally registering performance gains of around 1%. On TotalSegmentator, we achieve a Dice score of 93.51% with only 295 MB peak GPU memory. Zero-shot cross-dataset evaluations on SegTHOR and AMOS22 demonstrate strong generalization, with Dice scores of up to 86.85% and 89.35%, respectively. SegMate variants in this study empower single GPU setups to process up to 10,000 volumes per hour with just 74 J per volume using batch inference, enabling population-scale CT processing on commodity hardware. We release our open-source code at https://github.com/andreibunea99/SegMate.	research	en	2026-11-09 05:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:22:59.395661+00	4	\N	4ff2ce3d2a8a2cb099f123ee323cf1e1a989bfb638802e9fd0cf862efb29b17d	processed	2026-11-09 17:22:59.396115+00	2026-11-10 15:31:47.410008+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
d9ada8fc-e0b2-4869-9b4d-f076b360260d	d3342e2c-5c4d-4f89-a00d-09b38226d5e5	\N	https://openai.com/index/grid-protectors-program	Introducing the Grid Protectors Program	https://openai.com/index/grid-protectors-program	https://openai.com/index/grid-protectors-program	\N	OpenAI’s Grid Protectors Program will work with utilities to help future compute campuses support grid reliability and protect consumer electricity costs.	OpenAI’s Grid Protectors Program will work with utilities to help future compute campuses support grid reliability and protect consumer electricity costs.	product_update	en	2026-11-02 15:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:12:41.917407+00	3	\N	5fccaf1124cfa6a3ba56c670b8156a484497f3bac5af02983888a2ce747ed5d6	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:41.917824+00	2026-11-10 14:42:06.687421+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
