80b82802-dffb-4b46-afa0-6378e18aa24d	ffdef1b3-f1c0-4fa1-a6e3-8c350077f091	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.08771v1	Federated training performs as well as centralized for 3D Latent Diffusion for Diagnosis-Conditioned Brain MRI Synthesis	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.08771	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.08771	Abhijith Shaji, Paul Kurian, Greg Ver Steeg, Paul M. Thompson, Jose-Luis Ambite	arXiv:2611.08771v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: Generative models of brain MRI are useful to understand brain conditions, and to enrich scarce and imbalanced neuroimaging data. However, training these models requires large, multi-site training sets, which is challenging. Federated learning (FL) allows for training deep learning models without sharing data. We show that training a 3D conditional latent model federatedly (where data is kept private at each site) performs similarly to centralized training (where all the data have been copied to a single site). We evaluate three metrics: conditional fidelity (how well generated MRIs perform in classification), diversity (how the generated images match the real data distribution, using MultiScale-SSIM), and realism (how close generated images are to real images, using Fr\\'{e}chet Inception Distance). Our results show that federated training is a viable route to develop multi-site generative models of brain MRI.	arXiv:2611.08771v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: Generative models of brain MRI are useful to understand brain conditions, and to enrich scarce and imbalanced neuroimaging data. However, training these models requires large, multi-site training sets, which is challenging. Federated learning (FL) allows for training deep learning models without sharing data. We show that training a 3D conditional latent model federatedly (where data is kept private at each site) performs similarly to centralized training (where all the data have been copied to a single site). We evaluate three metrics: conditional fidelity (how well generated MRIs perform in classification), diversity (how the generated images match the real data distribution, using MultiScale-SSIM), and realism (how close generated images are to real images, using Fr\\'{e}chet Inception Distance). Our results show that federated training is a viable route to develop multi-site generative models of brain MRI.	research	en	2026-11-09 05:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:23:01.034969+00	4	\N	40a1e989d13c602f2b85aa52708698ba7ed574dffc608f961d7d403dcf30aa53	processed	2026-11-09 17:23:01.035492+00	2026-11-10 15:53:16.13145+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
42d401ee-faa6-4278-81c8-698a5eb1bcae	110c8b74-5d9a-4479-9380-aab19486cc0c	\N	https://deepmind.google/blog/engineering-more-resilient-crops-for-a-warming-climate/	Engineering more resilient crops for a warming climate	https://deepmind.google/blog/engineering-more-resilient-crops-for-a-warming-climate/	https://deepmind.google/blog/engineering-more-resilient-crops-for-a-warming-climate/	\N	Scientists are using AlphaFold to strengthen a photosynthesis enzyme for resilient, heat-tolerant crops.	Scientists are using AlphaFold to strengthen a photosynthesis enzyme for resilient, heat-tolerant crops.	research	en	2025-12-04 16:23:24+00	2026-11-09 17:12:35.350468+00	4	\N	7d3baf55761f488f516d11df81f3ae83b62af70ad5bab7e542b17f2f0e5dbe21	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:35.350912+00	2026-11-10 13:28:31.852129+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
