ad9699bb-1763-453c-b29d-fd2102e4028c	d58a9c86-f9be-4f8b-bd34-60f063fd344d	\N	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/1/delete-uv-lock-first/	If in doubt, delete the uv.lock file	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/1/delete-uv-lock-first/	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/1/delete-uv-lock-first/	\N	I've been getting the occasional confusing Python dependency error since switching over to Python 3.15 and the rule I'm having to remember is: If in doubt, delete the uv.lock file Most of my projects are libraries which don't include a uv.lock file, since it's rude for a library dependency to lock versions for anything else that uses it. Running uv run pytest etc tends to leave uv.lock files lying around, which are listed in .gitignore and so do not get committed to my repositories. But... sometimes that uv.lock pins a version of a dependency that doesn't yet have a Python 3.15 wheel. An example from earlier today: error: Failed to build `watchfiles==1.1.1`\n  cause: Call to `maturin.build_wheel` failed\n\nerror: the configured Python interpreter version (3.15) is newer\nthan PyO3's maximum supported version (3.14) Deleting that file and running uv run pytest again usually fixes the problem. Tags: uv , til , python	I've been getting the occasional confusing Python dependency error since switching over to Python 3.15 and the rule I'm having to remember is: If in doubt, delete the uv.lock file Most of my projects are libraries which don't include a uv.lock file, since it's rude for a library dependency to lock versions for anything else that uses it. Running uv run pytest etc tends to leave uv.lock files lying around, which are listed in .gitignore and so do not get committed to my repositories. But... sometimes that uv.lock pins a version of a dependency that doesn't yet have a Python 3.15 wheel. An example from earlier today: error: Failed to build `watchfiles==1.1.1`\n  cause: Call to `maturin.build_wheel` failed\n\nerror: the configured Python interpreter version (3.15) is newer\nthan PyO3's maximum supported version (3.14) Deleting that file and running uv run pytest again usually fixes the problem. Tags: uv , til , python	tutorial	en	2026-11-01 23:24:22+00	2026-11-09 17:12:46.869706+00	2	\N	fd07dadfd948b12d4101aed1c37f196614f3fedb547622cfdcf2f01fb6d3f40a	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:46.870143+00	2026-11-10 14:41:49.613962+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
