f80becac-676f-4af6-8935-4c9ebf6d018d	ffdef1b3-f1c0-4fa1-a6e3-8c350077f091	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.12550v1	A Strict Upper Bound for Three-Point Weighted Selection in Planar Vector-Valued Regression	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12550	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12550	Sergey Volkov	arXiv:2611.12550v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: We prove $F_{\\mathrm{weighted}}(2,2,3)<11/6$ for minimum-Frobenius-norm least-squares regression with two input and two output coordinates, improving the upper bound $15/8$. More precisely, a universal $\\varepsilon_0>0$ satisfies $\\mathcal T_3\\le(5/6-\\varepsilon_0)E$ for every finite residual frame. The proof combines an exact scalar certificate, rigidity of equality in planar selection, and a compactness argument that controls disappearing weights. Together with the known lower bound, this gives $13/8\\le F_{\\mathrm{weighted}}(2,2,3)<11/6$. No numerical value of $\\varepsilon_0$ is claimed.	arXiv:2611.12550v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: We prove $F_{\\mathrm{weighted}}(2,2,3)<11/6$ for minimum-Frobenius-norm least-squares regression with two input and two output coordinates, improving the upper bound $15/8$. More precisely, a universal $\\varepsilon_0>0$ satisfies $\\mathcal T_3\\le(5/6-\\varepsilon_0)E$ for every finite residual frame. The proof combines an exact scalar certificate, rigidity of equality in planar selection, and a compactness argument that controls disappearing weights. Together with the known lower bound, this gives $13/8\\le F_{\\mathrm{weighted}}(2,2,3)<11/6$. No numerical value of $\\varepsilon_0$ is claimed.	research	en	2026-11-10 05:00:00+00	2026-11-10 16:29:55.864094+00	3	\N	5743a87b2a86a2a2defa7570e7a2535a0bec24a130b0cf37f822f83802cf4aba	processed	2026-11-10 16:29:55.864447+00	2026-11-10 16:37:28.32362+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
