dcd7837e-9aa6-420d-8fd4-72b8df18a3e1	d58a9c86-f9be-4f8b-bd34-60f063fd344d	\N	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/27/game-boy-color-on-my-conference-badge/	Game Boy Color on My Conference Badge	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/27/game-boy-color-on-my-conference-badge/	https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/27/game-boy-color-on-my-conference-badge/	\N	Game Boy Color on My Conference Badge I'm at GitHub Universe this week and, similar to last year , the conference badge is a full-blown color screen computer. I've been hacking around with it again, and then I ran into with Steve Francia... who worked with Gemini to get a full NES emulator working on it, and then went a step further and deployed an emulator for both the Game Boy and the Game Boy Color. Which means, if you can obtain the ROM, you can run The Legend of Zelda: Link's Awakening on your conference badge! A neat feature of the badge is that you can turn it upside down and then use game controller touch buttons that are built into the badge body. Tags: games , github , hardware-hacking , ai , generative-ai , llms , gemini , steve-francia	Game Boy Color on My Conference Badge I'm at GitHub Universe this week and, similar to last year , the conference badge is a full-blown color screen computer. I've been hacking around with it again, and then I ran into with Steve Francia... who worked with Gemini to get a full NES emulator working on it, and then went a step further and deployed an emulator for both the Game Boy and the Game Boy Color. Which means, if you can obtain the ROM, you can run The Legend of Zelda: Link's Awakening on your conference badge! A neat feature of the badge is that you can turn it upside down and then use game controller touch buttons that are built into the badge body. Tags: games , github , hardware-hacking , ai , generative-ai , llms , gemini , steve-francia	news	en	2026-10-27 19:34:18+00	2026-11-09 17:12:46.928939+00	2	\N	21782f06bf8c08b298a5aed071a2902f704e2a4224a1fccf8bd353a001e2244e	proc