993708a8-39db-4e46-9ee5-5f9743a33103	ffdef1b3-f1c0-4fa1-a6e3-8c350077f091	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.11372v1	LLM-based Multi-Criteria Deep Reinforcement Learning for Dynamic Efficient 5G UPF Selection	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.11372	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.11372	Abdelrahman Soliman, Ahmed Refaey Hussein, Lei Lei	arXiv:2611.11372v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: User plane function (UPF) selection in 5G networks is an active area of research, with various limited approaches proposed to enhance network efficiency and manage resources effectively. In this paper, we address this gap in the related literature by proposing a Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) UPF selection method that utilizes a dynamic, multi-objective reward function and validating it on a real-world 5G emulation platform. The proposed method is based on the large language models' (LLMs) translation of network operator intents and the network data analytics function (NWDAF) abnormality alerts. The experimental results validated in the real-world experimental setup demonstrate that our dynamic DRL solution achieves an effective balance between latency, power consumption, and traffic distribution, outperforming the heuristic baselines and fixed DRL by 16.89%. These findings highlight the real-world applicability of our approach for dynamic, intent-driven UPF selection.	arXiv:2611.11372v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: User plane function (UPF) selection in 5G networks is an active area of research, with various limited approaches proposed to enhance network efficiency and manage resources effectively. In this paper, we address this gap in the related literature by proposing a Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) UPF selection method that utilizes a dynamic, multi-objective reward function and validating it on a real-world 5G emulation platform. The proposed method is based on the large language models' (LLMs) translation of network operator intents and the network data analytics function (NWDAF) abnormality alerts. The experimental results validated in the real-world experimental setup demonstrate that our dynamic DRL solution achieves an effective balance between latency, power consumption, and traffic distribution, outperforming the heuristic baselines and fixed DRL by 16.89%. These findings highlight the real-world applicability of our approach for dynamic, intent-driven UPF selection.	article	en	2026-11-10 05:00:00+00	2026-11-10 16:29:55.610686+00	\N	\N	db70ac1fa225e6beb03a02b85cb4cbfdc02ea1ff4c745c26b91d99e4fe5f5119	pending	2026-11-10 16:29:55.611013+00	2026-11-10 16:29:55.611015+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
