ff9045e3-b31a-4ba1-b479-ccc3f78a0465	928ad6da-fec1-474b-ae1a-3cf781cb4d3e	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.09417v1	Future-Informed Actor-Critic	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09417	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09417	Samy Mokeddem, Gaspard Lambrechts, Adrien Bolland, Damien Ernst	arXiv:2611.09417v1 Announce Type: new \nAbstract: Actor-critic methods optimize a parametrized policy using a critic to estimate their policy gradient. Recent work has shown that conditioning the critic on features of future states, actions, or rewards can improve sample efficiency and even final return. However, existing methods are restricted to exogenous features (independent of actions), overlooking endogenous features (dependent on actions) that may be crucial for credit assignment. We introduce the future-informed value function, which can be conditioned on both exogenous and endogenous features of future states, actions, and rewards. Then, we express the policy gradient using this value function, yielding the future-informed policy gradient. Building on that, we propose the future-informed actor-critic algorithm. Empirical results show that this algorithm leveraging endogenous features of the future outperforms standard actor-critic algorithms in environments with noisy and sparse rewards.	arXiv:2611.09417v1 Announce Type: new \nAbstract: Actor-critic methods optimize a parametrized policy using a critic to estimate their policy gradient. Recent work has shown that conditioning the critic on features of future states, actions, or rewards can improve sample efficiency and even final return. However, existing methods are restricted to exogenous features (independent of actions), overlooking endogenous features (dependent on actions) that may be crucial for credit assignment. We introduce the future-informed value function, which can be conditioned on both exogenous and endogenous features of future states, actions, and rewards. Then, we express the policy gradient using this value function, yielding the future-informed policy gradient. Building on that, we propose the future-informed actor-critic algorithm. Empirical results show that this algorithm leveraging endogenous features of the future outperforms standard actor-critic algorithms in environments with noisy and sparse rewards.	research	en	2026-11-09 05:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:22:58.532918+00	3	\N	c04d6041f897c73cbd2298d0c667395bc46f71d3912eea8fb91f390ac3a9a451	processed	2026-11-09 17:22:58.533329+00	2026-11-10 14:51:31.826037+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
