91ea4481-58dd-4e73-9d21-e5b3233447b9	d3342e2c-5c4d-4f89-a00d-09b38226d5e5	\N	https://openai.com/index/fanatics-streamline-fan-experience	How Fanatics and OpenAI streamline the fan experience	https://openai.com/index/fanatics-streamline-fan-experience	https://openai.com/index/fanatics-streamline-fan-experience	\N	Fanatics uses OpenAI to help fans complete their game-day outfits with Shop the Look. Testing across roughly 30,000 MLB products showed 10% higher engagement.	Fanatics uses OpenAI to help fans complete their game-day outfits with Shop the Look. Testing across roughly 30,000 MLB products showed 10% higher engagement.	product_update	en	2026-10-26 07:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:12:41.978688+00	3	\N	f6578a6ab7dee0ef02382669e208813424d70d3b36238adcef0f9eeee0a9ec70	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:41.979169+00	2026-11-10 14:39:50.509645+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
8cd5d9b7-9238-41d4-858a-d2b408ef42c3	d3342e2c-5c4d-4f89-a00d-09b38226d5e5	\N	https://openai.com/index/unlocking-new-ways-of-working	How workers are unlocking new ways of working	https://openai.com/index/unlocking-new-ways-of-working	https://openai.com/index/unlocking-new-ways-of-working	\N	New OpenAI Economic Research shows how workers use AI beyond traditional roles and which new activities become recurring parts of their work.	New OpenAI Economic Research shows how workers use AI beyond traditional roles and which new activities become recurring parts of their work.	research	en	2026-09-16 09:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:12:42.211431+00	3	\N	c90315cc2b847090be0fa3c38c1377fa4c4f4681337a3839ddc6589ff0fee71b	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:42.211863+00	2026-11-10 14:34:47.249537+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
4cbe5f08-4f5d-49b5-ab76-ee7f60a1f0e1	aa25b96e-953d-4a88-a929-27c2362afe1d	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2601.05903v2	HAPS: Hierarchical LLM Routing with Joint Architecture and Parameter Search	https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.05903	https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.05903	Zihang Tian, Rui Li, Jingsen Zhang, Xiaohe Bo, Wei Huo, Xu Chen	arXiv:2601.05903v2 Announce Type: replace \nAbstract: Large language model (LLM) routing aims to exploit the specialized strengths of different LLMs for diverse tasks. However, existing approaches typically focus only on selecting LLM architectures, treating candidate models as fixed while overlooking parameter adaptation, which can substantially affect task performance. In this paper, we introduce HAPS, a hierarchical LLM routing framework that jointly searches over model architectures and parameters. Specifically, a high-level router selects among candidate LLM architectures, while a low-level router generates input-conditioned LoRA parameters for the selected architecture, expanding each candidate from a single fixed behavior into a region of reachable behaviors. The low-level router is built on the backbone of the high-level router, so that architecture selection and parameter generation share a common representation of the prompt. We further optimize the whole framework with a reinforcement learning objective. Extensive experiments show that HAPS consistently outperforms strong routing baselines across reasoning- and knowledge-intensive benchmarks, with analyses of its components, design choices, scalability, cost, and mixed open- and closed-source deployment further demonstrating the robustness of these gains. Our code is available at https://github.com/zihangtian/HAPS.	arXiv:2601.05903v2 Announce Type: replace \nAbstract: Large language model (LLM) routing aims to exploit the specialized strengths of different LLMs for diverse tasks. However, existing approaches typically focus only on selecting LLM architectures, treating candidate models as fixed while overlooking parameter adaptation, which can substantially affect task performance. In this paper, we introduce HAPS, a hierarchical LLM routing framework that jointly searches over model architectures and parameters. Specifically, a high-level router selects among candidate LLM architectures, while a low-level router generates input-conditioned LoRA parameters for the selected architecture, expanding each candidate from a single fixed behavior into a region of reachable behaviors. The low-level router is built on the backbone of the high-level router, so that architecture selection and parameter generation share a common representation of the prompt. We further optimize the whole framework with a reinforcement learning objective. Extensive experiments show that HAPS consistently outperforms strong routing baselines across reasoning- and knowledge-intensive benchmarks, with analyses of its components, design choices, scalability, cost, and mixed open- and closed-source deployment further demonstrating the robustness of these gains. Our code is available at https://github.com/zihangtian/HAPS.	article	en	2026-11-10 05:00:00+00	2026-11-10 16:30:05.131051+00	\N	\N	53f8ee15d8417296d8df03785a5cc1056db33b178febf4e3be958a86803f5a7b	pending	2026-11-10 16:30:05.131343+00	2026-11-10 16:30:05.131344+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
