1ec736e2-698a-4180-bd1f-85c29bd8500c	d3342e2c-5c4d-4f89-a00d-09b38226d5e5	\N	https://openai.com/index/where-the-goblins-came-from	Where the goblins came from	https://openai.com/index/where-the-goblins-came-from	https://openai.com/index/where-the-goblins-came-from	\N	How goblin outputs spread in AI models: timeline, root cause, and fixes behind personality-driven quirks in GPT-5 behavior.	How goblin outputs spread in AI models: timeline, root cause, and fixes behind personality-driven quirks in GPT-5 behavior.	research	en	2026-04-29 20:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:12:42.830527+00	4	\N	8154000a5049e71fcdd4084012a00e03141f468b1fd84f30c0f93d849204f686	processed	2026-11-09 17:12:42.830897+00	2026-11-10 14:22:04.082021+00	pending	\N	\N	pending	0	\N	\N
ca3cf113-b7b6-4d92-b8ca-1f81737ad542	ffdef1b3-f1c0-4fa1-a6e3-8c350077f091	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.09271v1	Zero-Shot Weight-Space Programming Across a Difficulty-Graded Ladder of Two-Player Games	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09271	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09271	Eduardo C. Garrido-Merch\\'an	arXiv:2611.09271v1 Announce Type: new \nAbstract: Weight-space programming sets every weight of a feed-forward network by hand, from an explicit specification of the desired computation, with no gradient descent and no training data anywhere in the construction. We ask how far a large language model can carry this practice, zero-shot, across games of deliberately increasing difficulty. We design a four-rung ladder (Nim, tic-tac-toe, two sizes of Connect Four, and a chess endgame) spanning four axes of difficulty, and build a second, independent network at each rung, using a structurally unrelated game at matched difficulty, to separate what a rung's finding says about the difficulty level from what it says about the one game used to measure it. Ten networks are built and independently verified. Six admit a complete, non-statistical proof of correctness against an independent oracle. The chess-endgame rung is exact where correctness is cheap, move legality and, in one network, an exact one-ply mate detector, and collapses where it is expensive, composing a multi-move mating plan, from 84.1-100% success at the one-ply tactics it was built to get right down to 0.57-9.13% in full adversarial play; its replicate shows this collapse is an order of magnitude less severe under a shorter required plan and exact rather than heuristic safety checks. The standard-sized rung confirms, by holding hand-set evaluation weights fixed and adding only shallow search, that the remaining gap is an architectural ceiling rather than a matter of engineering effort, and this exact collapse reproduces across two structurally unrelated games. We release all ten networks, their independent oracles, construction-cost measurements, and a cold-prompt protocol for a future cross-model comparison	arXiv:2611.09271v1 Announce Type: new \nAbstract: Weight-space programming sets every weight of a feed-forward network by hand, from an explicit specification of the desired computation, with no gradient descent and no training data anywhere in the construction. We ask how far a large language model can carry this practice, zero-shot, across games of deliberately increasing difficulty. We design a four-rung ladder (Nim, tic-tac-toe, two sizes of Connect Four, and a chess endgame) spanning four axes of difficulty, and build a second, independent network at each rung, using a structurally unrelated game at matched difficulty, to separate what a rung's finding says about the difficulty level from what it says about the one game used to measure it. Ten networks are built and independently verified. Six admit a complete, non-statistical proof of correctness against an independent oracle. The chess-endgame rung is exact where correctness is cheap, move legality and, in one network, an exact one-ply mate detector, and collapses where it is expensive, composing a multi-move mating plan, from 84.1-100% success at the one-ply tactics it was built to get right down to 0.57-9.13% in full adversarial play; its replicate shows this collapse is an order of magnitude less severe under a shorter required plan and exact rather than heuristic safety checks. The standard-sized rung confirms, by holding hand-set evaluation weights fixed and adding only shallow search, that the remaining gap is an architectural ceiling rather than a matter of engineering effort, and this exact collapse reproduces across two structurally unrelated games. We release all ten networks, their independent oracles, construction-cost measurements, and a cold-prompt protocol for a future cross-model comparison	research	en	2026-11-09 05:00:00+00	2026-11-09 17:23:00.742967+00	3	\N	599dc376675578fe35e7ea7a66b5fea1ca0e25d669e2285de4840