3a7d3563-be79-48e5-bd2b-c546febea27b	928ad6da-fec1-474b-ae1a-3cf781cb4d3e	\N	oai:arXiv.org:2611.12375v1	AudioCodex: Streaming Autoencoders for Live Audio	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12375	https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12375	Marco Pasini, Javier Nistal, Cyran Aouameur, Stefan Lattner, George Fazekas	arXiv:2611.12375v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: We introduce AudioCodex, a fully causal autoencoder for live generative audio applications that compresses stereo audio into compact continuous latent sequences at ~10 Hz. It combines a Mean Flow magnitude autoencoder with latent hypersphere projection, bounded-noise augmentation, representation alignment, and adversarial phase recovery to learn representations that support both efficient downstream generation and high-quality reconstruction. Through extensive ablations, we show that AudioCodex outperforms the state-of-the-art in terms of generation-reconstruction trade-off, whilst remaining strictly causal in both encoding and decoding. This work paves the way towards truly real-time interactive and streaming generative audio applications.	arXiv:2611.12375v1 Announce Type: cross \nAbstract: We introduce AudioCodex, a fully causal autoencoder for live generative audio applications that compresses stereo audio into compact continuous latent sequences at ~10 Hz. It combines a Mean Flow magnitude autoencoder with latent hypersphere projection, bounded-noise augmentation, representation alignment, and adversarial phase recovery to learn representations that support both efficient downstream generation and high-quality reconstruction. Through extensive ablations, we show that AudioCodex outperforms the state-of-the-art in terms of generation-reconstruction trade-off, whilst remaining strictly causal in both encoding and decoding. This work paves the way towards truly real-time interactive and streaming generative audio applications.	article	en	2026-11-10 05:00:00+00	2026-11-10 16:30:02.712084+00	\N	\N	d28b19f2c406ec3b9790c2cef8ae